-- core.lut: primitive data and operations, their structural claims, and the core's
-- computable constructions (plane 3, D-2026-10-18-c; bite 6, prompt-bite-6.md at 2859815).
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-14, by Claude Fable 5.1, an agent of the coordinating session, on the brief
-- record/IA/slice-theories-2026-10-14/prompt.md (item 1 of the inventory's §6). Sources: spec
-- 11.R1 to 11.R3, 11.S4, 11.S5, 11.S7 (the numbers); 3.S7, 3.R2, 3.R3 (the core's data); 2.S12
-- (the translations that reach these names), 2.S21 (which words are keywords), 4.R13 (an
-- operator is resolved by the type of its operands); 12.S22 (`core.lut` encloses the top-level
-- scope of every file, so its names are visible unqualified); term.lth §5 (`Prim`: what the
-- kernel computes). The v0.1 file is `src/luthier/core.lut` at the tag v0.1-final.
--
-- Its name and its kind. The specification names this file `core.lut` (11.R2 allows `primitive`
-- here only; library.lth's policies anchor on the path); it is read as a model file by its
-- extension (library.lth, `KindByExtension`), which is its kind: it holds the interpreter's
-- values, not laws. Its laws live in theory files: core/structures/ states what `Unit`, `Empty`,
-- `Bool`, `Maybe` and `List` are, and core claims those theories for its data below
-- (D-2026-10-14-b); the end of this file names `Nat` and the kernel's forms as models (they were
-- kernel_models.lut's until the core's bite 1, 2026-10-18); numbers.lth states
-- what `Int`, `Float64` and `String` are, with numbers_model.lut naming the operations below as
-- models (12.S23, Z8). [proposed] That core is a `.lut` under `lib/` and not a third kind of
-- file; one commit undoes it.
--
-- What is not here. `extern`, `primitive` and `axiom` are names of core whose application the
-- checker recognizes (3.S39); they have no definition a file could write. The comparisons
-- `== /= < <= > >=` are the kernel's `Primitive` of the same symbol (3.S17, term.lth `Prim` and
-- its neighbours): the elaboration of `a < b` reaches `Primitive "<"` directly, since no act of
-- the grammar binds a comparison symbol (`operator` takes `+ - * / and or mod` only, 2.S9), and
-- `==` is one operation on every concrete type (4.R8). [proposed] So the comparisons are named
-- here in this comment and nowhere else; the arithmetic is named below and bound by `operator`.

import "core/lists.lut" appendList foldList mapKernelList lengthList atList
  all any count member lookup sum toList filter zipWith sameEntries pointwise supDistance entrywiseBall indicator
import "core/structures/universal.lth" Terminal Initial Coproduct Lists
  Exponential Product NamedProduct NamedCoproduct Selected one two
import "core/structures/algebraic.lth" TheBooleans Monoid Semiring CommutativeRing BooleanAlgebra
import "core/structures/order.lth" OrderedSemiring Order
import "core/structures/equality.lth" Concrete Structural Object Metric

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the core's data (3.S7, 3.R3)

-- the terminal and the initial structure, as data (3.S7; D-2026-10-13-t gives their roles in
-- core/structures/universal.lth: `unit` the point of a terminal object, `Empty` initial)
Unit : U := data { unit : Unit }
Empty : U := data { }

-- `Bool`: a sum of two units written as a `data` without recursion (3.R3, D-2026-10-13-o); its
-- role, a Boolean algebra with `true` its top, is core/structures/algebraic.lth §3, claimed below.
-- [proposed] `data` and not the labeled sum `{ true : Unit || false : Unit }` of 2.S12: 3.R3 is
-- the later decision, and the kernel represents `true` as the constructor `Var "true"`
-- (term.lth, `truth`), not as an injection.
Bool : U := data { true : Bool ; false : Bool }

-- the connectives: `a and b`, `a or b` and `p -> q` on Bools elaborate to these (2.S12); `and`
-- and `or` are operator words (2.S21), so their functions are named `conj` and `disj` and bound
-- by `operator` at `Bool` (4.R13)
not (b : Bool) : Bool := match b { true -> false ; false -> true }
conj (a b : Bool) : Bool := match a { true -> b ; false -> false }
disj (a b : Bool) : Bool := match a { true -> true ; false -> b }
implies (a b : Bool) : Bool := match a { true -> b ; false -> true }
operator and := conj
operator or := disj

-- `Maybe` and `List`, as data (3.R3, 3.S36); their roles: a coproduct with `Unit`
-- and the free monoid (core/structures/universal.lth §4), claimed below. `[a, b, c]`
-- is `cons a (cons b (cons c nil))` (2.S12).
Maybe (A : U) : U := data { nothing : Maybe A ; just : A -> Maybe A }
List (A : U) : U := data { nil : List A ; cons : A -> List A -> List A }

-- The roles of the data above (L2.7; D-2026-10-14-b: 4.R3 is read per file, and a data's role
-- laws live in the file that defines it, without repeating a law). Each data is the model of a
-- structure of core/structures/, and core claims that structure here: the law is that file's,
-- applied to core's model written with the constructors. `unit` is the point of a terminal
-- object; `true` and `false` the top and bottom of a Boolean algebra, `true` where `if` takes its
-- first branch; `nothing` and `just` the injections of a coproduct with `Unit`; `nil` the neutral
-- element of the free monoid and `cons` the injection combined. `Empty` has no constructor to
-- give a role to; it is initial, its elimination `match e { }` the map out. Moved from
-- kernel_models.lut. [proposed] Importing core/structures/ from core is a cycle of files and not of
-- names: core/structures/ sees core's names unqualified (12.S22) and core names its theories, but
-- no definition reaches itself through the other file (the theories mention `Bool` and `List`, the
-- data mention no theory), and a demand reads definitions, not files (3.S1, 12.S22).
unitIsTerminalModel  : Terminal Unit (structural Unit) := { point := unit }
UnitIsTerminal (equality : Object Unit <- structural Unit) (model : Terminal Unit equality <- { point := unit }) : Bool := Terminal Unit equality model
emptyIsInitialModel  : Initial Empty := { absurd := fn (A : U) (e : Empty) { match e { } } }
EmptyIsInitial  (model : Initial Empty <- { absurd := fn (A : U) (e : Empty) { match e { } } }) : Bool := Initial Empty model
boolIsTheBooleansModel  : TheBooleans := { algebra := { top := true, bottom := false, complement := fn b { not b }, meet := fn a b { conj a b }, join := fn a b { disj a b } } }
BoolIsTheBooleans  (model : TheBooleans <- { algebra := { top := true, bottom := false, complement := fn b { not b }, meet := fn a b { conj a b }, join := fn a b { disj a b } } }) : Bool := TheBooleans model
boolIsACoproductModel  : Coproduct Unit Unit Bool (structural Bool) := { left := fn u { true }, right := fn u { false }, cases := fn (C : U) f g b { if b then f unit else g unit } }
BoolIsACoproduct  (model : Coproduct Unit Unit Bool (structural Bool) <- { left := fn u { true }, right := fn u { false }, cases := fn (C : U) f g b { if b then f unit else g unit } }) : Bool := Coproduct Unit Unit Bool (structural Bool) model
maybeIsACoproductModel (A : Concrete) : Coproduct Unit A (Maybe A) (structural (Maybe A)) := { left := fn u { nothing }, right := fn a { just a }, cases := fn (C : U) f g m { match m { nothing -> f unit ; just a -> g a } } }
MaybeIsACoproduct (A : Concrete) (model : Coproduct Unit A (Maybe A) (structural (Maybe A)) <- { left := fn u { nothing }, right := fn a { just a }, cases := fn (C : U) f g m { match m { nothing -> f unit ; just a -> g a } } }) : Bool := Coproduct Unit A (Maybe A) (structural (Maybe A)) model
listIsTheFreeMonoidModel (A : Concrete) : Lists A (structural (List A)) := { free := { monoid := { neutral := nil, combine := appendList A }, inject := fn a { cons a nil }, foldable := { fold := foldList } } }
ListIsTheFreeMonoid (A : Concrete) (model : Lists A (structural (List A)) <- { free := { monoid := { neutral := nil, combine := appendList A }, inject := fn a { cons a nil }, foldable := { fold := foldList } } }) : Bool := Lists A (structural (List A)) model
foldInto (A N : U) (n : Monoid N (structural N)) (f : A -> N) (xs : List A) : N :=
  match xs { nil -> n.neutral ; cons a rest -> n.combine (f a) (foldInto A N n f rest) }


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the primitive types (11.R1, 11.S4)

-- Each body says what it is (11.R1). `Int` is the integers without bound, realized exactly by
-- the host's; `Real` the ideal, which nothing computes (its structure is the axiom `realField`
-- of numbers_model.lut, 11.R3); `Float64` the finite doubles, every one a real number, so it
-- refines `Real`, with the machine's rounded operations (11.S4: the refinement is of the values,
-- not of the operations); `Rational` the rationals, exactly, refining `Real`, with no literal
-- (its values come from `lib/rational.lut`, 11.S4, not written); `String` is text.
Int      : U := primitive "integer"
Real     : U := primitive "real"
Float64  : Real := primitive "ieee754-binary64"
Rational : Real := primitive "rational"
String   : U := primitive "unicode"

-- the naturals and the finite type of `n` indices (11.R1): subtypes of `Int`, so neither has a
-- constructor of its own; `Nat`'s laws are core/structures/algebraic.lth §5
Nat : U := { k : Int | 0 <= k }
Fin (n : Int) : U := { k : Int | 0 <= k and k < n }

-- an infinity that means something is asked for in the type (11.S7); nothing else is one
ExtendedReal = { finite : Float64 || negInf : Unit || posInf : Unit }

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the operations (3.S17, 11.S4, 11.S5)

-- The kernel computes these on constants (3.S17; term.lth §5 states each step). Each is a
-- `primitive` body named by its symbol, as term.lth's `Prim` writes them (`Primitive "+"`), typed
-- at one type, and the infix symbol is bound to it by `operator` at that type (4.R13, 2.R2: a
-- type names its model; `Int + Int` and `Float64 + Float64` are two models of one symbol).
-- What each one is: numbers.lth (`Doubles`, `IntegerDivision`, `Conversion`; the ring of `Int`
-- in algebra.lth) and core/structures/algebraic.lth (`Monoid` for `String`).

-- the integers: exact (11.S4); the quotient and the remainder are the host's floor division,
-- `(a / b) * b + a mod b == a` with the remainder taking the sign of the divisor
-- (numbers.lth `IntegerDivision`); a zero divisor is an error and no term (term.lth `PrimInt`)
intPlus  : Int -> Int -> Int := primitive "+"
intMinus : Int -> Int -> Int := primitive "-"
intTimes : Int -> Int -> Int := primitive "*"
intDiv   : Int -> Int -> Int := primitive "/"
intMod   : Int -> Int -> Int := primitive "mod"
operator + := intPlus
operator - := intMinus
operator * := intTimes
operator / := intDiv
operator mod := intMod

-- the doubles: the machine's rounded operations (11.S4), each the IEEE 754 operation in
-- round-to-nearest; NaN and an overflow are errors, never values (11.S7)
floatPlus   : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64 := primitive "+"
floatMinus  : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64 := primitive "-"
floatTimes  : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64 := primitive "*"
floatDivide : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64 := primitive "/"
operator + := floatPlus
operator - := floatMinus
operator * := floatTimes
operator / := floatDivide

-- text: `+` is concatenation, the free monoid on characters (core/structures/algebraic.lth `Monoid`,
-- numbers_model.lut `strings`)
stringAppend : String -> String -> String := primitive "+"
operator + := stringAppend

-- the nearest double to an integer, exact below 2^53; the name stays with the integers
-- (11.S5, D-2026-10-05-c). Here and not in a library, since every program that draws a double
-- from an integer needs it (v0.1 real.lut bound it to the host for the same reason).
toFloat64 : Int -> Float64 := primitive "toFloat64"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the kernel's own models (kernel_models.lut)

-- What kernel_models.lut held until the core's bite 1 (2026-10-18), moved here with its text and
-- names unchanged (D-2026-10-14-b read to the end: core claims its models, and the kernel's forms
-- are the interpreter's; record/plan/core-2026-10-17/execution.md §3.10, whose renames come in bite
-- 3). Its draft 0 was by Claude Opus 5.5 in the session, 2026-10-13 (step 2.1; §7 of
-- kernel_laws.lth): each value says which known structure a core type or a kernel form is (L2.7,
-- D-2026-10-13-t).

-- the structural equality of every concrete type is an object (D-2026-10-12-ak, 4.R8)
structuralEquality (A : Concrete) : Structural A := { eq := fn x y { x == y } }

-- `Nat` is an ordered commutative semiring (11.R1)
naturals : OrderedSemiring Nat (structural Nat) := {
  semiring := { zero := 0, one := 1, plus := fn a b { a + b }, times := fn a b { a * b } },
  order := { leq := fn a b { a <= b } } }

-- the kernel's application, pairing and match are the exponential, the product and the coproduct
-- (3.S8, 3.S36); on `Bool` and `Maybe` the coproduct is core.lut's
application (A B : Concrete) : Exponential A B (structural B) := { apply := fn f x { f x } }
pairs (A B : Concrete) : Product A B (A * B) (structural A) (structural B) (structural (A * B)) := {
  pair := fn a b { (a, b) },
  first := fn p { match p { (a, b) -> a } },
  second := fn p { match p { (a, b) -> b } },
}
-- a record type is a named product: `.x` and `.y` its projections (D-2026-10-13-x); a labeled sum a
-- named coproduct, its labels the injections. Instances on the labels `x`, `y` and `one`, `two`.
-- [proposed, the core's bite 1] `sumAB`'s labels were `a` and `b` in kernel_models.lut, which no
-- file imported; in core every program loads them, and a label reserves its name in every file of
-- the program (run.py's `Loaded`), so a user's `a` or `b` would be renamed `a@file` (the record's
-- plan in test_run.py showed it). `one` and `two` are `Selected`'s, loaded with core already.
recordXY (A B : Concrete) : NamedProduct A B { x : A, y : B } (structural A) (structural B) (structural { x : A, y : B }) := {
  pair := fn u v { { x := u, y := v } },
  first := fn r { r.x }, second := fn r { r.y },
  firstName := "x", secondName := "y",
  select := fn n r { if n == "x" then just (one r.x) else if n == "y" then just (two r.y) else nothing },
}
sumAB (A B : Concrete) : NamedCoproduct A B { one : A || two : B } (structural { one : A || two : B }) := {
  left := fn u { one u }, right := fn v { two v },
  cases := fn (C : U) f g s { match s { one u -> f u ; two v -> g v } },
  leftName := "one", rightName := "two",
  labelOf := fn s { match s { one u -> "one" ; two v -> "two" } },
}

-- Computable combinators (D-2026-10-18-c, plane 3), moved from properties/functions.lth.
id (A : U) : A -> A := fn x { x }
compose (A B C : U) (g : B -> C) (f : A -> B) : A -> C := fn x { g (f x) }
flip (A B C : U) (f : A -> B -> C) : B -> A -> C := fn b a { f a b }
const (A B : U) (b : B) : A -> B := fn a { b }


-- Computable models and helpers, plane 3 (D-2026-10-18-c).
structural (A : Concrete) : Object A := { eq := fn x y { x == y } }
asObject (A : Concrete) (s : Structural A) : Object A := { eq := s.eq }
floatAbs (x : Float64) : Float64 := if x < 0.0 then 0.0 - x else x
MetricTolerance (A : U) (d : A -> A -> Float64) (epsilon : NonNegativeFloat) : A -> A -> Bool := fn x y { d x y <= epsilon }

intIsAnObjectModel  : Object Int := structural Int
IntIsAnObject  (model : Object Int <- structural Int) : Bool := Object Int model
natIsAnObjectModel  : Object Nat := structural Nat
NatIsAnObject  (model : Object Nat <- structural Nat) : Bool := Object Nat model
boolIsAnObjectModel  : Object Bool := structural Bool
BoolIsAnObject  (model : Object Bool <- structural Bool) : Bool := Object Bool model
stringIsAnObjectModel  : Object String := structural String
StringIsAnObject  (model : Object String <- structural String) : Bool := Object String model
floatIsAnObjectModel  : Object Float64 := structural Float64
FloatIsAnObject  (model : Object Float64 <- structural Float64) : Bool := Object Float64 model
intIsASemiringModel  : Semiring Int (structural Int) := { zero := 0, one := 1, plus := intPlus, times := intTimes }
IntIsASemiring  (model : Semiring Int (structural Int) <- { zero := 0, one := 1, plus := intPlus, times := intTimes }) : Bool := Semiring Int (structural Int) model
intIsACommutativeRingModel  : CommutativeRing Int (structural Int) := { zero := 0, one := 1, plus := intPlus, times := intTimes, negate := fn x { 0 - x } }
IntIsACommutativeRing  (model : CommutativeRing Int (structural Int) <- { zero := 0, one := 1, plus := intPlus, times := intTimes, negate := fn x { 0 - x } }) : Bool := CommutativeRing Int (structural Int) model
intIsOrderedModel  : Order Int (structural Int) := { leq := fn a b { a <= b } }
IntIsOrdered  (model : Order Int (structural Int) <- { leq := fn a b { a <= b } }) : Bool := Order Int (structural Int) model
natIsOrderedModel  : Order Nat (structural Nat) := { leq := fn a b { a <= b } }
NatIsOrdered  (model : Order Nat (structural Nat) <- { leq := fn a b { a <= b } }) : Bool := Order Nat (structural Nat) model
boolIsOrderedModel  : Order Bool (structural Bool) := { leq := fn a b { not a or b } }
BoolIsOrdered  (model : Order Bool (structural Bool) <- { leq := fn a b { not a or b } }) : Bool := Order Bool (structural Bool) model
stringIsOrderedModel  : Order String (structural String) := { leq := extern "python:operator.le" }
StringIsOrdered  (model : Order String (structural String) <- { leq := extern "python:operator.le" }) : Bool := Order String (structural String) model
floatIsOrderedModel  : Order Float64 (structural Float64) := { leq := fn a b { a <= b } }
FloatIsOrdered  (model : Order Float64 (structural Float64) <- { leq := fn a b { a <= b } }) : Bool := Order Float64 (structural Float64) model
natIsAnOrderedSemiringModel  : OrderedSemiring Nat (structural Nat) := naturals
NatIsAnOrderedSemiring  (model : OrderedSemiring Nat (structural Nat) <- naturals) : Bool := OrderedSemiring Nat (structural Nat) model
stringIsAMonoidModel  : Monoid String (structural String) := { neutral := "", combine := stringAppend }
StringIsAMonoid  (model : Monoid String (structural String) <- { neutral := "", combine := stringAppend }) : Bool := Monoid String (structural String) model
boolIsABooleanAlgebraModel  : BooleanAlgebra Bool (structural Bool) := { top := true, bottom := false, complement := not, meet := conj, join := disj }
BoolIsABooleanAlgebra  (model : BooleanAlgebra Bool (structural Bool) <- { top := true, bottom := false, complement := not, meet := conj, join := disj }) : Bool := BooleanAlgebra Bool (structural Bool) model
-- The Float64-valued integer distance is exact on MetricInteger, not on unbounded Int
-- distances. This bound belongs to the carrier, not a silent testing restriction (11.S4).
MetricInteger : U := { k : Int | -4503599627370496 <= k and k <= 4503599627370496 }
intIsAMetricModel  : Metric MetricInteger (structural MetricInteger) := { d := fn x y { floatAbs (toFloat64 (x - y)) } }
IntIsAMetric  (model : Metric MetricInteger (structural MetricInteger) <- { d := fn x y { floatAbs (toFloat64 (x - y)) } }) : Bool := Metric MetricInteger (structural MetricInteger) model
boolIsAMetricModel  : Metric Bool (structural Bool) := { d := fn x y { if x == y then 0.0 else 1.0 } }
BoolIsAMetric  (model : Metric Bool (structural Bool) <- { d := fn x y { if x == y then 0.0 else 1.0 } }) : Bool := Metric Bool (structural Bool) model
kernelAppliesModel (A B : Concrete) : Exponential A B (structural B) := application A B
KernelApplies (A B : Concrete) (model : Exponential A B (structural B) <- application A B) : Bool := Exponential A B (structural B) model
pairsAreTheProductModel (A B : Concrete) : Product A B (A * B) (structural A) (structural B) (structural (A * B)) := pairs A B
PairsAreTheProduct (A B : Concrete) (model : Product A B (A * B) (structural A) (structural B) (structural (A * B)) <- pairs A B) : Bool := Product A B (A * B) (structural A) (structural B) (structural (A * B)) model
recordsAreNamedProductsModel (A B : Concrete) : NamedProduct A B { x : A, y : B } (structural A) (structural B) (structural { x : A, y : B }) := recordXY A B
RecordsAreNamedProducts (A B : Concrete) (model : NamedProduct A B { x : A, y : B } (structural A) (structural B) (structural { x : A, y : B }) <- recordXY A B) : Bool := NamedProduct A B { x : A, y : B } (structural A) (structural B) (structural { x : A, y : B }) model
sumsAreNamedCoproductsModel (A B : Concrete) : NamedCoproduct A B ({ one : A || two : B }) (structural ({ one : A || two : B })) := sumAB A B
SumsAreNamedCoproducts (A B : Concrete) (model : NamedCoproduct A B ({ one : A || two : B }) (structural ({ one : A || two : B })) <- sumAB A B) : Bool := NamedCoproduct A B ({ one : A || two : B }) (structural ({ one : A || two : B })) model
CoreData := UnitIsTerminal & EmptyIsInitial & BoolIsTheBooleans & BoolIsACoproduct & MaybeIsACoproduct
  & ListIsTheFreeMonoid & IntIsAnObject & NatIsAnObject & BoolIsAnObject & StringIsAnObject & FloatIsAnObject
  & IntIsASemiring & IntIsACommutativeRing & IntIsOrdered & NatIsOrdered & BoolIsOrdered & StringIsOrdered
  & FloatIsOrdered & NatIsAnOrderedSemiring & StringIsAMonoid & BoolIsABooleanAlgebra
  & IntIsAMetric & BoolIsAMetric & KernelApplies & PairsAreTheProduct & RecordsAreNamedProducts & SumsAreNamedCoproducts
  & FinIsACoequalizer & SubtypeIsAnEqualizer

-- Finite folds, moved from arrays.lth §2 (same right association).
foldFrom (A : U) (op : A -> A -> A) (unit : A) (n : Int) (lo : Nat) (f : Fin n -> A) : A :=
  if lo >= n then unit else op (f lo) (foldFrom A op unit n (lo + 1) f)
foldWith (A : U) (op : A -> A -> A) (unit : A) (n : Int) (f : Fin n -> A) : A := foldFrom A op unit n 0 f

-- spec 3.S27: the sum of n doubles is `f 0 + (f 1 + (... + (f (n - 1) + 0.0)))`; the order is
-- part of the definition, and every specimen keeps it.
sumTo (n : Int) (f : Fin n -> Float64) : Float64 := foldWith Float64 (fn a b { a + b }) 0.0 n f
sumToInt (n : Int) (f : Fin n -> Int) : Int := foldWith Int (fn a b { a + b }) 0 n f
-- a law over every index, some index, every pair of indices below n: the closure, evaluated
forallBelow (n : Int) (p : Fin n -> Bool) : Bool := foldWith Bool (fn a b { a and b }) true n p
existsBelow (n : Int) (p : Fin n -> Bool) : Bool := foldWith Bool (fn a b { a or b }) false n p
forallPairs (n : Int) (p : Fin n -> Fin n -> Bool) : Bool := forallBelow n (fn i { forallBelow n (p i) })
countBelow (n : Int) (p : Fin n -> Bool) : Int := sumToInt n (fn k { if p k then 1 else 0 })

-- Generic finite container computations (execution.md §3.4; D-2026-10-18-c plane 3).



-- Minimal container models for kernel name resolution; bite 7 extends lists.lut.
ListIsAFunctor (model : Functor List <- { map := mapKernelList }) : Bool := Functor List model
ListIsIndexed (A : Concrete) (model : Indexed (List A) A <- { size := lengthList A, at := atList A }) : Bool := Indexed (List A) A model
ListIsAnObject (A : Concrete) (model : Object (List A) <- structural (List A)) : Bool := Object (List A) model
FinIsACoequalizer (n : { n : Int | 0 < n })
  (model : Coequalizer Int (Fin n) (structural (Fin n)) (fn a b { a mod n == b mod n }) <- {
    project := fn a { a mod n }, representative := fn k { k }, lift := fn (B : U) b f respect k { f k } }) : Bool :=
  Coequalizer Int (Fin n) (structural (Fin n)) (fn a b { a mod n == b mod n }) model
SubtypeIsAnEqualizer (A : Concrete) (predicate : A -> Bool)
  (model : Equalizer A Bool { x : A | predicate x } (structural A) (structural Bool) (structural { x : A | predicate x }) predicate (fn x { true }) <- {
    include := fn x { x }, restrict := fn x { x } }) : Bool :=
  Equalizer A Bool { x : A | predicate x } (structural A) (structural Bool) (structural { x : A | predicate x }) predicate (fn x { true }) model
CoreConstructions := ListIsAFunctor & ListIsIndexed & ListIsAnObject & FinIsACoequalizer & SubtypeIsAnEqualizer

-- Kernel type instances of the generic properties (moved from bite 2 test scaffolding).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- relations.lth at Int

IntReflexive (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (x : Int) : Bool := Reflexive Int r x
IntIrreflexive (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (x : Int) : Bool := Irreflexive Int r x
IntSymmetric (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (p : Related Int r) : Bool := Symmetric Int r p
IntAntisymmetric (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (x y : Int) : Bool := Antisymmetric Int (structural Int) r x y
IntAsymmetric (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (p : Related Int r) : Bool := Asymmetric Int r p
IntTransitive (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (c : Chain Int r) : Bool := Transitive Int r c
IntTotal (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (x y : Int) : Bool := Total Int r x y
IntEquivalence (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) := Equivalence Int r
IntPreorder (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) := Preorder Int r
IntPartialOrder (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) := PartialOrder Int (structural Int) r
IntTotalOrder (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) := TotalOrder Int (structural Int) r
IntStrictOrder (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) := StrictOrder Int r
-- antisymmetry as a premise over `Both`, so that the subtype is drawn too
IntBothWaysEqual (r : Int -> Int -> Bool) (b : Both Int r) : Bool := b.x == b.y

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- operations.lth at Int, Bool, String

IntAssociative (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (x y z : Int) : Bool := Associative Int (structural Int) op x y z
IntCommutative (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (x y : Int) : Bool := Commutative Int Int (structural Int) op x y
IntIdempotent (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Idempotent Int (structural Int) op x
IntLeftNeutral (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (e : Int) (x : Int) : Bool := LeftNeutral Int (structural Int) op e x
IntRightNeutral (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (e : Int) (x : Int) : Bool := RightNeutral Int (structural Int) op e x
IntNeutral (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (e : Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Neutral Int (structural Int) op e x
IntAbsorbing (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (z : Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Absorbing Int (structural Int) op z x
IntCancellative (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (x y z : Int) : Bool := Cancellative Int (structural Int) op x y z
IntInvertible (op : Int -> Int -> Int) (e : Int) (inv : Int -> Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Invertible Int (structural Int) op e inv x
IntDistributive (product sum : Int -> Int -> Int) (x y z : Int) : Bool := Distributive Int (structural Int) product sum x y z
IntAbsorptive (meet join : Int -> Int -> Int) (x y : Int) : Bool := Absorptive Int (structural Int) meet join x y
IntDistinct (a b : Int) : Bool := Distinct Int (structural Int) a b

BoolAssociative (op : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (x y z : Bool) : Bool := Associative Bool (structural Bool) op x y z
BoolCommutative (op : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (x y : Bool) : Bool := Commutative Bool Bool (structural Bool) op x y
BoolIdempotent (op : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (x : Bool) : Bool := Idempotent Bool (structural Bool) op x
BoolNeutral (op : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (e : Bool) (x : Bool) : Bool := Neutral Bool (structural Bool) op e x
BoolAbsorbing (op : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (z : Bool) (x : Bool) : Bool := Absorbing Bool (structural Bool) op z x
BoolDistributive (product sum : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (x y z : Bool) : Bool := Distributive Bool (structural Bool) product sum x y z
BoolAbsorptive (meet join : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (x y : Bool) : Bool := Absorptive Bool (structural Bool) meet join x y
-- the complement reaches the operation's absorbing element: `false` for `and`, `true` for `or`
BoolComplemented (op : Bool -> Bool -> Bool) (complement : Bool -> Bool) (z : Bool) (x : Bool) : Bool :=
  Complemented Bool (structural Bool) op complement z x

StringAssociative (op : String -> String -> String) (x y z : String) : Bool := Associative String (structural String) op x y z
StringCommutative (op : String -> String -> String) (x y : String) : Bool := Commutative String String (structural String) op x y
StringNeutral (op : String -> String -> String) (e : String) (x : String) : Bool := Neutral String (structural String) op e x

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the within-bound laws at Float64

FloatAssociativeWithin (op : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (bound3 : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (x y z : Float64) : Bool :=
  AssociativeWithin Float64 coreFloatDistance op bound3 x y z
FloatCommutativeWithin (op : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (bound2 : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (x y : Float64) : Bool :=
  CommutativeWithin Float64 Float64 coreFloatDistance op bound2 x y
FloatNeutralWithin (op : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (e : Float64) (bound1 : Float64 -> Float64) (x : Float64) : Bool :=
  NeutralWithin Float64 coreFloatDistance op e bound1 x
FloatDistributiveWithin (product sum : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (bound3 : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (x y z : Float64) : Bool :=
  DistributiveWithin Float64 coreFloatDistance product sum bound3 x y z
FloatInvertibleWithin (op : Float64 -> Float64 -> Float64) (e : Float64) (inv : Float64 -> Float64) (bound1 : Float64 -> Float64) (x : Float64) : Bool :=
  InvertibleWithin Float64 coreFloatDistance op e inv bound1 x

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- functions.lth at Int, Bool, Float64

IntPointwise (f g : Int -> Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Pointwise Int Int (structural Int) f g x
IntPointwise2 (f g : Int -> Int -> Int) (x y : Int) : Bool := Pointwise2 Int Int Int (structural Int) f g x y
IntInjective (f : Int -> Int) (x y : Int) : Bool := Injective Int Int (structural Int) (structural Int) f x y
BoolInjective (f : Bool -> Bool) (x y : Bool) : Bool := Injective Bool Bool (structural Bool) (structural Bool) f x y
IntSurjective (f s : Int -> Int) (y : Int) : Bool := Surjective Int Int (structural Int) f s y
IntInverse (f g : Int -> Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Inverse Int Int (structural Int) f g x
IntIsomorphism (to from : Int -> Int) := Isomorphism Int Int (structural Int) (structural Int) to from
IntBijective (f s : Int -> Int) := Bijective Int Int (structural Int) (structural Int) f s
IntIdempotentFunction (f : Int -> Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Pointwise Int Int (structural Int) (compose Int Int Int f f) f x
IntInvolutive (f : Int -> Int) (x : Int) : Bool := Involutive Int (structural Int) f x
BoolInvolutive (f : Bool -> Bool) (x : Bool) : Bool := Involutive Bool (structural Bool) f x
IntMonotone (r t : Int -> Int -> Bool) (f : Int -> Int) (p : Related Int r) : Bool := Monotone Int Int r t f p
IntPreserving (opA opB : Int -> Int -> Int) (f : Int -> Int) (x y : Int) : Bool := Preserving Int Int (structural Int) opA opB f x y
IntCongruent (rA : Int -> Int -> Bool) (f : Int -> Int) (p : Related Int rA) : Bool := Congruent Int Int rA (structural Int) f p
IntLandsIn (f : Int -> Int) (inside : Int -> Bool) (x : Int) : Bool := LandsIn Int Int f inside x

FloatIdempotentWithin (f : Float64 -> Float64) (bound1 : Float64 -> Float64) (x : Float64) : Bool := IdempotentWithin Float64 coreFloatDistance f bound1 x
FloatInvolutiveWithin (f : Float64 -> Float64) (bound1 : Float64 -> Float64) (x : Float64) : Bool := InvolutiveWithin Float64 coreFloatDistance f bound1 x
FloatPointwiseWithin (f g : Float64 -> Float64) (bound1 : Float64 -> Float64) (x : Float64) : Bool := PointwiseWithin Float64 Float64 coreFloatDistance f g bound1 x

coreFloatDistance (a b : Float64) : Float64 := floatAbs (a - b)
CoreProperties := IntReflexive & IntIrreflexive & IntSymmetric & IntAntisymmetric & IntAsymmetric & IntTransitive & IntTotal & IntEquivalence & IntPreorder & IntPartialOrder & IntTotalOrder & IntStrictOrder & IntBothWaysEqual & IntAssociative & IntCommutative & IntIdempotent & IntLeftNeutral & IntRightNeutral & IntNeutral & IntAbsorbing & IntCancellative & IntInvertible & IntDistributive & IntAbsorptive & IntDistinct & BoolAssociative & BoolCommutative & BoolIdempotent & BoolNeutral & BoolAbsorbing & BoolDistributive & BoolAbsorptive & BoolComplemented & StringAssociative & StringCommutative & StringNeutral & FloatAssociativeWithin & FloatCommutativeWithin & FloatNeutralWithin & FloatDistributiveWithin & FloatInvertibleWithin & IntPointwise & IntPointwise2 & IntInjective & BoolInjective & IntSurjective & IntInverse & IntIsomorphism & IntBijective & IntIdempotentFunction & IntInvolutive & BoolInvolutive & IntMonotone & IntPreserving & IntCongruent & IntLandsIn & FloatIdempotentWithin & FloatInvolutiveWithin & FloatPointwiseWithin

KernelFiniteQuantifiers (n : Nat) (model : FiniteQuantifiers n <- { every := forallBelow n, some := existsBelow n, pairs := forallPairs n }) : Bool := FiniteQuantifiers n model
KernelQueries (F : U -> U) (folding : Foldable F) (model : FoldableQueries F folding <- { every := fn (A : U) { all F A folding }, contains := fn (A : U) { member F A folding } }) : Bool := FoldableQueries F folding model
KernelEntrywise (C A : U) (i : Indexed C A) (d : A -> A -> Float64)
  (candidate : ((c : C) -> C -> Fin (i.size c) -> Float64) -> C -> C -> Bool <- entrywiseBall C A i d) :=
  EntrywiseSpecification C A i d candidate
KernelImplication (candidate : Bool -> Bool -> Bool <- implies) := MaterialImplication candidate
CoreComputations := KernelFiniteQuantifiers & KernelQueries & KernelEntrywise & KernelImplication
